# What must never enter the build context.
#
# Two of these are correctness, not tidiness.
#
# `node_modules` carries platform-native binaries built for the host machine;
# copying them into a Linux image produces failures that read as dependency
# problems and are not. The image installs its own.
#
# `apps/api/data` is the LOCAL DATABASE. It holds seeded host api_key_hash
# values and whatever traveller data this machine has. Baking it into an image
# would ship real credentials to a registry, and would also mean the deployed
# app starts on a copy of somebody's laptop instead of an empty volume.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store
apps/api/data

# Build output. The image builds its own web bundle; a stale dist copied in
# could be a DEMO build, which would answer from a snapshot behind a URL
# claiming to be the real API.
dist*/
**/dist*/
build/
.expo
**/.expo

# Deploy identity and secrets. Never.
.env
.env.*
.vercel
**/.vercel

# History and tooling the runtime has no use for.
.git
.gitignore
.github
docs
contract
*.md
!README.md

# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea
.vscode
*.log
